Step 3: Create cPanel Mailboxes
Store configuration:
config/cpanel.conf
[cpanel]
server=100.125.194.89
token=YOUR_TOKEN
domain=linoop.us
Example API call:
import requests

url="https://100.125.194.89:2083/execute/Email/add_pop"

payload={
    "email":"sajjad.shafiq",
    "domain":"linoop.us",
    "password":"Welcome@123",
    "quota":"1024"
}

headers={
    "Authorization":"cpanel root:TOKEN"
}

r=requests.post(
    url,
    headers=headers,
    data=payload,
    verify=False
)

print(r.json())
Loop through the CSV and create all mailboxes.
________________________________________
Step 4: Create Active Directory Users
If AD is on Windows, PowerShell is usually easier than Python.
create_ad.ps1
Import-Csv users.csv | ForEach-Object {

    $username = $_.FullName.ToLower().Replace(" ",".")

    $password = ConvertTo-SecureString `
      "Welcome@123" `
      -AsPlainText `
      -Force

    New-ADUser `
      -Name $_.FullName `
      -SamAccountName $username `
      -UserPrincipalName "$username@corp.linoop.us" `
      -AccountPassword $password `
      -Enabled $true `
      -ChangePasswordAtLogon $true
}
Run:
.\create_ad.ps1
________________________________________
Step 5: Create Zoom Accounts
Create a Server-to-Server OAuth app in Zoom.
create_zoom.py
import requests

headers={
  "Authorization":"Bearer TOKEN"
}

payload={
    "action":"create",
    "user_info":{
        "email":"sajjad.shafiq@linoop.us",
        "type":1,
        "first_name":"Sajjad",
        "last_name":"Shafiq"
    }
}

requests.post(
    "https://api.zoom.us/v2/users",
    json=payload,
    headers=headers
)
Loop through all users.
