Even Simpler Approach
For only 17 users, you could:
1.	Keep everything in a single CSV. 
2.	Write one Python script. 
3.	The script: 
o	Reads CSV 
o	Generates usernames 
o	Generates random passwords 
o	Creates cPanel mailbox via API 
o	Creates Zoom user via API 
o	Writes a CSV report 
4.	Export a second CSV for AD and import it with a PowerShell script. 
This "Python + PowerShell" approach is often simpler to maintain than Ansible when the task is user onboarding rather than server configuration management.







Would this approach work if I have 150 users.
Yes, absolutely. For 150 users, a Python-based onboarding system is actually more practical than manually creating accounts and scales very well.
However, once you get into 150+ users, I'd recommend making a few improvements instead of using the simple scripts I showed earlier.
What Changes for 150 Users?
Instead of:
users.csv
      ↓
Create User
      ↓
Next User
Build:
users.csv
      ↓
Validation
      ↓
Username Generation
      ↓
Password Generation
      ↓
Create Mailbox
      ↓
Create AD Account
      ↓
Create Zoom Account
      ↓
Generate Report
      ↓
Send Welcome Email
________________________________________
Use a Master CSV
Example:
FullName,PersonalEmail,Department
Sajjad Shafiq,sajroman@gmail.com,IT
Khawar Abbas,khawarjora@gmail.com,IT
Usman Bhatti,usmanbh3@gmail.com,Support
The CSV becomes your source of truth.
________________________________________
Generate a Report
For 150 users you'll want:
FullName,Username,Mailbox,AD,Zoom,Status
Sajjad Shafiq,sajjad.shafiq,Created,Created,Created,Success
Khawar Abbas,khawar.abbas,Created,Failed,Created,Partial
This helps identify failures and rerun only the failed accounts.
________________________________________
Implement Logging
Create:
logs/onboarding.log
Example:
2026-05-29 10:15:01
Created cPanel mailbox:
sajjad.shafiq@linoop.us

2026-05-29 10:15:05
Created AD user:
sajjad.shafiq@corp.linoop.us
If user #89 fails, you can see exactly where.
________________________________________
Handle Duplicate Names
With 150 users, duplicates become likely.
Example:
Muhammad Ali
Muhammad Ali
Instead of:
muhammad.ali
muhammad.ali
Automatically generate:
muhammad.ali
muhammad.ali1
or
muhammad.ali
muhammad.ali2
________________________________________
Generate Strong Passwords
Don't use:
Welcome@123
Use something like:
Xk9!Lm7#Qa2P
Store it in the report.
Example:
Username,Password
sajjad.shafiq,Xk9!Lm7#Qa2P
Protect this file carefully.
________________________________________
Use Retry Logic
For APIs:
for attempt in range(3):
    try:
        create_zoom_user()
        break
    except:
        time.sleep(5)
If Zoom or cPanel has a temporary issue, the script retries automatically.
________________________________________
Send Emails at the End
Bad:
Create User
Send Email

Create User
Send Email
Better:
Create All Users
Generate Report
Verify Success
Send Emails
This avoids emailing credentials for accounts that failed to provision completely.
